<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the signed/notarized macOS build.

  disable-library-validation lets a DAW host (which has its own Team ID) load our
  plug-in bundle, and lets the bundle load its embedded JUCE code, under the hardened
  runtime. Without it, hosts signed by a different team refuse to load the plug-in.

  device.audio-input is REQUIRED for the Standalone to capture from an interface
  under the hardened runtime. Without it macOS disables audio input for the process
  outright: no TCC permission prompt ever appears and the input callback delivers
  silence, while output (and the settings panel's TEST tone) keep working. That was
  the v0.1.6-v0.2.0 Standalone "dead input VU" bug (TalkBass p3, ardgedee) - every
  notarized build lacked it; the last ad-hoc-signed build (v0.1.5) didn't need it.
  The NSMicrophoneUsageDescription string set in CMakeLists (MICROPHONE_PERMISSION_*)
  is still required too: the entitlement enables the capability, TCC + that string
  governs the user-facing permission prompt. Both must be present.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
